  "question": {
    "text": "The difference in oxidation state of chromium in chromate and dichromate salts is___",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p>Let the oxidation number of chromium be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>The oxidation state of chromium in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>So, the oxidation number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>also</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the difference in oxidation number between ions is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
